# The Linux packaging files are read by dpkg/rpm and by the desktop
# environment, none of which tolerate CRLF — a postinst starting `#!/bin/sh\r`
# fails with an error that names neither the file nor the reason. Pin them so a
# checkout on a Windows machine with core.autocrlf=true cannot break the build.
src-tauri/linux/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
